- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/api-http-methods.md`: Export functions named after HTTP methods to handle different request types.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/api-middleware.md`: Implement middleware patterns for authentication, logging, and other cross-cutting concerns.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/api-query-params.md`: Access URL query parameters using the URL API in Next.js Route Handlers.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/api-rate-limiting.md`: Implement rate limiting to protect your API from abuse and ensure fair usage.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/api-request-body.md`: Next.js Route Handlers use the Web Request API for parsing request bodies.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/api-response-types.md`: Return different response types from Route Handlers based on your needs.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/api-route-handlers.md`: CRA typically uses a separate backend or proxied API. Next.js provides built-in API routes.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/assets-absolute-urls.md`: In Next.js, reference files in the `public` folder directly without any prefix or environment variable.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/assets-favicon.md`: Next.js App Router supports placing favicon files directly in the `app` directory for automatic handling.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/assets-manifest.md`: Next.js App Router can generate the web app manifest dynamically or use a static file.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/assets-public-folder.md`: The `public/` folder works identically in Next.js and CRA. Files are served from the root URL.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/assets-static-imports.md`: Import images and other assets directly for automatic optimization and type safety.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/build-bundle-analysis.md`: Analyze your bundle to identify large dependencies and optimization opportunities.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/build-docker.md`: Deploy Next.js in Docker containers for Kubernetes, AWS ECS, or other container platforms.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/build-output.md`: CRA and Next.js produce different build outputs with different deployment requirements.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/build-scripts.md`: Replace CRA's react-scripts with Next.js build commands.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/build-standalone.md`: Use standalone output for smaller, self-contained deployments (Docker, custom servers).
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/build-static-export.md`: Export your Next.js app as a static site, similar to CRA's build output.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/build-vercel.md`: Vercel is the recommended platform for deploying Next.js applications.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-boundary-placement.md`: Push `'use client'` boundaries as low as possible in the component tree to minimize client JavaScript.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-children-pattern.md`: Use the children prop to pass Server Components into Client Components, preserving their server-rendered benefits.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-composition.md`: Use component composition to keep Server Components for static content while Client Components handle interactivity.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-context-providers.md`: React Context uses `useContext` which requires `'use client'`. Wrap providers at the right level in your app.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-interleaving.md`: Server and Client Components can be mixed throughout your component tree. Understand the rendering rules.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-props-serialization.md`: Props passed from Server Components to Client Components must be serializable (convertible to JSON).
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-server-default.md`: In Next.js App Router, all components are Server Components by default. This is a key paradigm shift from CRA.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-third-party.md`: Many third-party libraries export Client Components that need `'use client'`. Create wrapper components to use them in Server Components.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/components-use-client.md`: In Next.js App Router, components are Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` for components that need browser APIs or React hooks.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-caching.md`: Next.js extends the native fetch API with caching options. Understand the defaults and how to override them.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-client-fetch.md`: Some data fetching must remain client-side (user interactions, real-time updates). Use proper patterns like SWR or React Query.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-client-library-init.md`: Module-level initialization of client-only libraries runs on the server where browser APIs may not be available. Initialize these libraries in a client component's useEffect instead.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-parallel-fetching.md`: When fetching multiple independent pieces of data, fetch them in parallel to avoid waterfalls.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-revalidation.md`: Next.js provides multiple revalidation strategies to control when cached data is refreshed.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-sequential-fetching.md`: When one fetch depends on another's result, handle the sequence properly while still optimizing where possible.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-server-actions.md`: CRA handles form submissions with client-side fetch. Next.js Server Actions provide a simpler pattern for mutations.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-streaming.md`: Next.js supports streaming HTML with Suspense, allowing parts of the page to load progressively.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-useeffect-to-rsc.md`: CRA fetches data in useEffect on the client. Next.js Server Components can fetch data directly during render on the server.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-useeffect-to-ssg.md`: For static content that doesn't change often, use `getStaticProps` to fetch data at build time.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/data-useeffect-to-ssr.md`: For Pages Router migrations, use `getServerSideProps` for server-side data fetching on every request.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/deps-react19-compatibility.md`: Next.js 14+ with React 19 requires major version upgrades for several common packages. These packages will fail or show warnings if not upgraded.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/env-build-time.md`: Environment variables in Next.js are inlined at build time, not read at runtime by default.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/env-local-files.md`: Next.js loads environment files in a specific order, which differs slightly from CRA.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/env-prefix-change.md`: CRA uses `REACT_APP_` prefix for browser-exposed variables. Next.js uses `NEXT_PUBLIC_`.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/env-runtime-config.md`: For values that need to change without rebuilding, use runtime configuration instead of build-time env vars.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/env-server-only.md`: Variables without `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix are only available on the server, keeping secrets secure.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/env-validation.md`: Validate environment variables at build/startup time to catch configuration errors early.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/fonts-font-display.md`: Configure how fonts are displayed while loading with the `display` option.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/fonts-google-fonts.md`: Use `next/font/google` to load Google Fonts with automatic optimization.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/fonts-local-fonts.md`: Use `next/font/local` to load custom font files with the same optimization benefits.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/fonts-next-font.md`: Replace CSS font imports with `next/font` for automatic optimization and zero layout shift.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/fonts-preload.md`: Next.js automatically preloads fonts configured with `next/font`. No manual preload links needed.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/fonts-variable-fonts.md`: Variable fonts provide all weights in a single file, improving performance.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-api-routes-edge.md`: Next.js API routes can run on Edge or Node.js runtime. Know the differences.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-auth-race-conditions.md`: The most critical migration issue: API calls executing before authentication or configuration is ready. In CRA, everything loads client-side so timing is predictable. In Next.js with SSR, components may render before async configuration completes.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-auth-state-gating.md`: Always wait for authentication to complete before checking roles or permissions. During initial render, auth state is typically undefined, causing premature redirects.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-configuration-idempotency.md`: Prevent duplicate initialization of services using refs. React 18+ StrictMode intentionally double-invokes effects in development, and Fast Refresh can re-run initialization code.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-cookies.md`: Cookies work differently in Server Components, Route Handlers, and Client Components.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-dynamic-imports.md`: Use `next/dynamic` for code splitting and client-only components instead of React.lazy.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-empty-modules.md`: TypeScript's `isolatedModules` option (enabled by default in Next.js) requires every file to have at least one import or export statement.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-headers.md`: Setting response headers works differently in various Next.js contexts.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-hydration-mismatch.md`: Hydration errors occur when server HTML doesn't match client render. Debug and fix them.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-hydration-nested-interactive.md`: Nesting interactive elements (button inside a link, link inside a button) causes hydration errors in Next.js. The browser's HTML parser corrects invalid nesting, creating a mismatch between server-rendered and client-rendered HTML.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-infinite-rerender.md`: Object and array references change on every render. Using them directly as `useEffect` dependencies causes infinite re-render loops.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-middleware.md`: Next.js Middleware always runs on the Edge runtime, which has limitations.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-nullish-coalescing.md`: Complex expressions using nullish coalescing (`??`) can cause `_variable is not defined` runtime errors in Next.js due to how the code is transpiled.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-provider-hierarchy.md`: Provider order matters. Providers can only access context from providers above them in the tree. Incorrect ordering causes runtime errors, styling issues, or missing context.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-react19-class-components.md`: React 19 changes how `this` is bound in certain callback contexts, causing `this` to be `undefined` in Promise `.then()` handlers, `setState` callbacks, and nested callbacks within class components.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-react19-ref-prop.md`: React 19 changes how refs work: `ref` is now a regular prop, and
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-redirect.md`: Next.js has multiple ways to redirect. Choose the right one for your use case.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-router-push-timing.md`: Calling `router.push()` during the render phase causes React errors. Navigation must happen in event handlers or effects, not in the component body.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-router-ready.md`: In Pages Router, query params aren't available during SSR. Check `isReady` before using them.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-static-generation.md`: Understanding when Next.js renders statically vs dynamically is crucial for performance.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-turbopack.md`: Next.js 16+ uses Turbopack as the default bundler for development. Some webpack-specific features are not supported.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-use-effect-timing.md`: useEffect behavior in Next.js differs from CRA due to Server Components and SSR.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-websocket-optional-deps.md`: When migrating CRA apps that use `socket.io-client` or `ws` for WebSocket connections, you may encounter bundling errors due to optional native dependencies.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/gotchas-window-undefined.md`: The most common migration issue: `window` and `document` don't exist during server-side rendering.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-fill-prop.md`: Use the `fill` prop when you want images to fill their parent container responsively.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-loader.md`: Use custom loaders when using image CDNs like Cloudinary, Imgix, or custom solutions.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-next-image.md`: Replace HTML `<img>` tags with Next.js `<Image>` component for automatic optimization.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-optimization.md`: Next.js automatically optimizes images on-demand. Understand how it works.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-placeholder.md`: Use blur placeholders to improve perceived performance while images load.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-priority.md`: Add `priority` to images that are the Largest Contentful Paint (LCP) element for better performance.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-remote-patterns.md`: External images must be explicitly allowed in `next.config.js` for security.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/images-required-dimensions.md`: Next.js Image requires width and height to prevent Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS).
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/integrations-sentry.md`: Replace `@sentry/browser` or `@sentry/react` with `@sentry/nextjs` for proper Next.js integration.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-basic-pages.md`: CRA uses React Router for routing. Next.js uses file-based routing where the file path determines the URL.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-catch-all-routes.md`: React Router uses `*` for catch-all routes. Next.js uses `[...slug]` folder syntax.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-dynamic-routes.md`: React Router uses `:param` syntax. Next.js uses `[param]` folder names for dynamic route segments.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-error-boundaries.md`: CRA requires manual Error Boundaries. Next.js provides automatic error handling via `error.tsx` files.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-hash-based.md`: Some CRA applications use hash-based routing (`#/path` or `#key=value`) for client-side state that shouldn't trigger server requests. This pattern requires special handling in Next.js.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-intercepting-routes.md`: Intercepting routes let you show a route in a modal while keeping the background context, with the full page accessible via direct URL.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-link-component.md`: React Router's `Link` must be replaced with Next.js's `Link` component from `next/link`.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-loading-states.md`: CRA requires manual loading states. Next.js provides automatic loading UI via `loading.tsx` files.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-nested-layouts.md`: React Router uses `<Outlet />` for nested routes. Next.js uses `layout.tsx` files that wrap child routes.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-not-found.md`: CRA handles 404s with a catch-all route. Next.js uses `not-found.tsx` files for custom 404 pages.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-optional-catch-all.md`: When you need to match both the base route AND all sub-routes, use optional catch-all `[[...slug]]`.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-parallel-routes.md`: Parallel routes allow rendering multiple pages in the same layout simultaneously, useful for dashboards, modals, or split views.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-programmatic-navigation.md`: React Router's `useNavigate` hook is replaced by Next.js's `useRouter` from `next/navigation`.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-protected-routes.md`: Next.js offers multiple patterns for route protection. Choose based on whether you need client-side or server-side protection.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-route-groups.md`: CRA organizes routes in code. Next.js uses `(group)` folders to organize routes without affecting the URL structure.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-use-params.md`: React Router's `useParams` hook is replaced by the `params` prop passed to page components in Next.js.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/routing-use-search-params.md`: React Router's `useSearchParams` differs from Next.js's implementation.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-canonical.md`: Set canonical URLs to prevent duplicate content issues with search engines.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-dynamic-metadata.md`: Use `generateMetadata` function for pages with dynamic content (blog posts, products, etc.).
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-head-component.md`: When migrating from Pages Router to App Router, replace `next/head` with the Metadata API.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-json-ld.md`: Add JSON-LD structured data for rich search results in Google.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-metadata-api.md`: Replace `react-helmet` or `react-helmet-async` with Next.js's built-in Metadata API.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-opengraph.md`: Configure Open Graph metadata for rich social media previews.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-robots.md`: Control how search engines index your pages with robots meta tags.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-sitemap.md`: Generate a sitemap dynamically to help search engines discover and index your pages.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/seo-twitter-cards.md`: Configure Twitter Card metadata for rich previews on Twitter/X.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/setup-eslint.md`: CRA includes ESLint via react-scripts. Next.js provides its own ESLint configuration with Next.js-specific rules.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/setup-gitignore.md`: CRA and Next.js have different build output directories that should be ignored.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/setup-initial-structure.md`: CRA uses a flat `src/` structure with manual routing. Next.js App Router uses a `app/` directory where folders define routes.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/setup-next-config.md`: CRA uses `react-scripts` with limited configuration (via `craco` or ejecting). Next.js uses `next.config.js` for all configuration.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/setup-package-json.md`: CRA includes react-scripts which bundles all tooling. Next.js requires explicit dependencies and different scripts.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/setup-typescript.md`: CRA's TypeScript setup differs from Next.js. Next.js will auto-generate a compatible `tsconfig.json` on first run.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-context-client.md`: React Context uses hooks which require `'use client'`. Provider components must be Client Components.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-jotai.md`: Jotai has excellent Next.js support with minimal configuration needed.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-persistence.md`: Handle localStorage and sessionStorage properly to avoid hydration issues.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-recoil.md`: Recoil requires wrapping your app in `RecoilRoot` with a Client Component.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-redux.md`: Redux requires special configuration for Next.js to handle server-side rendering properly.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-server-state.md`: Server Components eliminate the need for much client-side state. Rethink what truly needs to be client state.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-url-state.md`: Use URL search params for state that should be shareable, bookmarkable, or persist across refreshes.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/state-zustand.md`: Zustand works in Next.js but needs care to avoid hydration mismatches.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-component-styles.md`: In Next.js App Router, component-level CSS must use CSS Modules, not global CSS imports.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-css-import-order.md`: CSS import order in your layout files determines the cascade. Styles imported later override earlier ones when specificity is equal. This matters more in Next.js because all CSS is bundled together.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-css-in-js.md`: CSS-in-JS libraries need special configuration for Server-Side Rendering in Next.js.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-css-modules.md`: CSS Modules work almost identically in Next.js. The main difference is file naming convention.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-dark-mode-hydration.md`: Dark mode implementations that read from localStorage during render cause hydration mismatches. The server doesn't have access to localStorage, so it renders a different theme than the client.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-emotion.md`: Emotion requires specific configuration for Next.js App Router to prevent flash of unstyled content.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-global-css.md`: CRA imports global CSS in `index.tsx`. Next.js App Router imports global CSS in the root `layout.tsx`.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-postcss.md`: PostCSS configuration in Next.js works the same as in CRA with a `postcss.config.js` file.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-sass.md`: CRA includes Sass support after installing `sass`. Next.js works the same way.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-scss-global-syntax.md`: The `:global` syntax is a CSS Modules feature. It only works in `.module.scss` files, not regular `.scss` files. Next.js enforces this more strictly than CRA.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-styled-components.md`: styled-components requires specific configuration to work with Next.js Server-Side Rendering.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/styling-tailwind.md`: Tailwind CSS configuration in Next.js requires updating content paths for the App Router structure.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-api-routes.md`: Test Route Handlers by calling them directly or using integration tests.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-async-components.md`: Test components that fetch data asynchronously using proper async patterns.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-client-components.md`: Client Components are tested similarly to CRA components, but may need Next.js mocks.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-e2e-cypress.md`: Configure Cypress for end-to-end testing of your Next.js application.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-e2e-playwright.md`: Configure Playwright for fast, reliable end-to-end testing.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-jest-config.md`: CRA includes Jest configuration. Next.js requires explicit setup.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-mocking.md`: Common patterns for mocking Next.js specific modules in tests.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-react-testing-library.md`: React Testing Library works the same way in Next.js for Client Components.
- `.claude/skills/cra-to-next-migration/rules/testing-server-components.md`: Server Components require different testing approaches since they're async and run on the server.

