- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/link-universal-links-ios.md`: Universal Links open your app when users tap links to your website. Requires hosting an `apple-app-site-association` file.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/route-drawer-navigator.md`: Use the Drawer navigator for apps with a side menu. Requires `react-native-reanimated` and `react-native-gesture-handler`.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/route-dynamic-segments.md`: Use square brackets `[param]` in filenames to create dynamic route segments. Access parameters with `useLocalSearchParams()`.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/route-file-based-routing.md`: Expo Router uses file-based routing where files in the `app/` directory automatically become routes. Every screen is automatically deep linkable.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/route-modal-presentation.md`: Use the `presentation: 'modal'` option to present screens as overlays. Modals are useful for forms, confirmations, and focused tasks.
