- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/screen-detail-params.md`: Pass only the ID via route params, then fetch full data on the detail screen. Passing entire objects leads to stale data and serialization issues.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/screen-header-options.md`: Use `options` on Stack.Screen for static config or `useNavigation().setOptions()` for dynamic updates based on data.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/screen-list-flashlist.md`: FlashList recycles components under the hood for dramatically better performance, especially on Android. It's a drop-in replacement for FlatList.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/screen-loading-state.md`: Always handle loading, error, and empty states. Users should never see a blank screen or wonder if the app is working.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/screen-pull-to-refresh.md`: Pull-to-refresh is an expected interaction on mobile lists. Use RefreshControl with FlashList or FlatList.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/screen-settings-list.md`: Use SectionList for settings screens with grouped options. This follows native platform conventions.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/setup-app-config-typescript.md`: Use `app.config.ts` instead of `app.json` for type-safe configuration with autocomplete and compile-time validation.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/setup-development-build.md`: Expo Go is a sandbox for prototyping but cannot use custom native modules. Development builds are your own version of Expo Go with full native code access.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/setup-eas-build-profiles.md`: Define separate build profiles in `eas.json` for development, preview, and production environments with appropriate settings for each.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/setup-environment-variables.md`: Only variables prefixed with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are inlined into the client bundle. Never prefix sensitive secrets with `EXPO_PUBLIC_` as end users can access all embedded environment variables.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/setup-typescript-config.md`: Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json to catch type errors before runtime. Expo has first-class TypeScript support with the `expo/tsconfig.base` preset.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/test-component-testing.md`: Use `@testing-library/react-native` for testing components the way users interact with them.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/test-e2e-maestro.md`: Use Maestro for end-to-end testing. It's recommended by Expo and integrates with EAS Workflows.
- `.claude/skills/expo-react-native-coder/references/test-error-boundary.md`: Use error boundaries to catch JavaScript errors in components and display fallback UI instead of crashing.
