- `.claude/skills/graph-schema/references/anti-duplicate-data.md`: Copying data between nodes (e.g., storing company name on every Employee node) is a relational-world habit. In graphs, you traverse: the company name lives on the Company node, and every Employee reaches it via the WORKS_AT relationship. Duplicated data becomes stale and inconsistent the moment t...
