## PHP Best Practices

PHP 8.x modern patterns, PSR standards, and SOLID principles. Use when reviewing PHP code, checking type safety, auditing code quality, or ensuring PHP best practices. Triggers on "review PHP", "check PHP code", "audit PHP", or "PHP best practices".

- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/SKILL.md`
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/AGENTS.md`: **Version:** 2.1.0 **Focus:** PHP 8.0 - 8.5, PSR Standards, Modern PHP Features **Rules:** 51 (9 type + 16 modern + 6 PSR + 5 SOLID + 5 error + 5 perf + 5 security) **License:** MIT
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/README.md`: Modern PHP 8.x patterns, PSR standards, and SOLID principles for clean, maintainable code.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/_sections.md`: This file defines all sections, their ordering, impact levels, and descriptions. The section ID (in parentheses) is the filename prefix used to group rules.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/_template.md`: **Impact: MEDIUM (optional impact description)**
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/error-custom-exceptions.md`: Create specific exception classes for different error scenarios instead of using generic exceptions.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/error-exception-hierarchy.md`: Organize exceptions into a meaningful hierarchy so callers can catch at different levels of specificity.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/error-finally-cleanup.md`: Use `finally` blocks to guarantee cleanup code runs whether an exception occurs or not.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/error-never-suppress.md`: Never use the `@` error suppression operator. Handle errors explicitly instead.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/error-try-catch-specific.md`: Always catch the most specific exception type possible. Never catch generic `\Exception` or `\Throwable` unless at the top-level error boundary.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-arrow-functions.md`: Use arrow functions for short, single-expression closures (PHP 7.4+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-asymmetric-visibility.md`: Use asymmetric visibility to allow public reading but restrict writing (PHP 8.4+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-attributes.md`: Use native attributes for metadata instead of docblock annotations (PHP 8.0+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-constructor-promotion.md`: Constructor property promotion (PHP 8.0+) reduces boilerplate code significantly. It combines parameter declaration, property declaration, and assignment into a single statement, making classes cleaner and easier to maintain.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-enums-methods.md`: Add methods to enums to encapsulate related behavior and logic.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-enums.md`: Enums (PHP 8.1+) provide type-safe constants with methods. They prevent invalid values, enable IDE autocompletion, and encapsulate related behavior. Always prefer enums over class constants for finite sets of values.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-first-class-callables.md`: Use first-class callable syntax to create closures from callables (PHP 8.1+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-match-expression.md`: Use match expressions instead of switch statements for cleaner, safer code (PHP 8.0+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-named-arguments.md`: Use named arguments for clarity and flexibility (PHP 8.0+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-nullsafe-operator.md`: Use the nullsafe operator for cleaner null checking chains (PHP 8.0+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-override-attribute.md`: Use `#[\Override]` on methods that override a parent method (PHP 8.3+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-pipe-operator.md`: Use the pipe operator (`|>`) for readable function chaining (PHP 8.5+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-property-hooks.md`: Use property hooks to define get/set logic directly on properties (PHP 8.4+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-readonly-classes.md`: Use readonly classes when all properties should be immutable (PHP 8.2+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-readonly-properties.md`: Use readonly properties for immutable data that should only be set once (PHP 8.1+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/modern-typed-constants.md`: Use typed class constants to enforce type safety on constant values (PHP 8.3+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/perf-array-functions.md`: Use PHP's built-in array functions instead of manual loops. They are implemented in C and significantly faster.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/perf-avoid-globals.md`: Never use global variables or the `global` keyword. Use dependency injection instead.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/perf-generators.md`: Use generators (`yield`) to process large datasets without loading everything into memory.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/perf-lazy-loading.md`: Load resources and perform expensive operations only when they are actually needed, not at construction time.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/perf-string-functions.md`: Use PHP's built-in string functions instead of regex for simple operations. String functions are faster and more readable.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/psr-12-coding-style.md`: Follow PSR-12 extended coding style for consistent, readable code.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/psr-4-autoloading.md`: Follow PSR-4 autoloading standard for class file organization.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/psr-file-structure.md`: Organize PHP files with proper ordering of elements and logical grouping.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/psr-namespace-usage.md`: Use namespaces properly to organize code and avoid naming conflicts.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/psr-naming-classes.md`: Use PascalCase for class names with descriptive, intention-revealing names.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/psr-naming-methods.md`: Use camelCase for method names with clear, action-oriented verbs.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/sec-file-uploads.md`: Always validate file type, size, and name. Store uploads outside the web root or in non-executable locations.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/sec-input-validation.md`: Always validate and sanitize all external input before using it. Never trust data from users, APIs, or any external source.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/sec-output-escaping.md`: Always escape output based on the context where it will be used to prevent XSS and injection attacks.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/sec-password-hashing.md`: Always use `password_hash()` and `password_verify()` for password security. Never use MD5, SHA1, or plain text.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/sec-sql-prepared.md`: Always use prepared statements with parameter binding for SQL queries. Never concatenate user input into SQL strings.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/solid-dip.md`: High-level modules should not depend on low-level modules. Both should depend on abstractions.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/solid-isp.md`: Clients should not be forced to depend on interfaces they do not use.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/solid-lsp.md`: Subtypes must be substitutable for their base types without altering correctness.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/solid-ocp.md`: Classes should be open for extension but closed for modification.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/solid-srp.md`: A class should have only one reason to change - one responsibility.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-intersection-types.md`: Use intersection types when a value must implement multiple interfaces (PHP 8.1+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-mixed-avoid.md`: Avoid using mixed type; prefer specific types or union types instead.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-nullable-types.md`: Use nullable types explicitly when null is a valid value.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-parameter-types.md`: Always declare types for all function and method parameters.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-property-types.md`: Always declare types for class properties (PHP 7.4+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-return-types.md`: Always declare return types for all methods and functions.
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-strict-mode.md`
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-union-types.md`: Use union types when a value can legitimately be one of multiple types (PHP 8.0+).
- `.claude/skills/php-best-practices/rules/type-void-never.md`: Use void for methods that don't return a value, and never for methods that always throw or exit.

