- `.claude/skills/ruby-on-rails-best-practices/rules/thin-controllers.md`: Controllers should be thin orchestrators that call rich model APIs directly. Avoid service objects, interactors, or other intermediaries between controllers and models.
- `.claude/skills/ruby-on-rails-best-practices/rules/thin-jobs.md`: Jobs should be thin wrappers that receive records and call model methods. All business logic belongs in the model layer.
