- `.claude/skills/storefront-best-practices/reference/components/footer.md`: Footer provides supplementary navigation, company info, and trust signals. Appears on every page.
- `.claude/skills/storefront-best-practices/reference/components/hero.md`: Hero section is the prominent banner at top of homepage, immediately below navigation. First content users see - sets tone for shopping experience.
- `.claude/skills/storefront-best-practices/reference/components/megamenu.md`: Megamenu is a large, full-width dropdown navigation showing multiple columns of categories, links, and promotional content. Opens from navbar trigger items (e.g., "Shop", "Men", "Women").
- `.claude/skills/storefront-best-practices/reference/components/navbar.md`: Primary navigation for ecommerce storefronts. Desktop: horizontal menu with category links. Mobile: hamburger drawer with accordion subcategories.
- `.claude/skills/storefront-best-practices/reference/components/popups.md`: Popups (modals/overlays) appear over main content to capture attention for specific actions: newsletter signups, promotional offers, exit-intent offers.
- `.claude/skills/storefront-best-practices/reference/components/product-card.md`: Product cards display products in grids (product listings, search results, related products). Key ecommerce considerations: clear pricing, quick add-to-cart, and stock indicators.
