## User Interface Wiki

UI/UX best practices for web interfaces. Use when reviewing animations, CSS, audio, typography, UX patterns, prefetching, or icon implementations. Covers 11 categories from animation principles to typography. Outputs file:line findings.

- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/SKILL.md`
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/AGENTS.md`: **Version 3.0.0** raphael-salaja March 2026
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/_sections.md`: This file defines all sections, their ordering, impact levels, and descriptions. The section ID (in parentheses) is the filename prefix used to group rules.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/_template.md`: Brief explanation of the rule and why it matters.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/a11y-reduced-motion-check.md`: Respect prefers-reduced-motion as proxy for sound sensitivity.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/a11y-toggle-setting.md`: Provide explicit toggle to disable sounds in settings.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/a11y-visual-equivalent.md`: Every audio cue must have a visual equivalent; sound never replaces visual feedback.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/a11y-volume-control.md`: Allow volume adjustment independent of system volume.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/appropriate-confirmations-only.md`: Sound is appropriate for confirmations: payments, uploads, form submissions.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/appropriate-errors-warnings.md`: Sound is appropriate for errors and warnings that can't be overlooked.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/appropriate-no-decorative.md`: Do not add sound to decorative moments with no informational value.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/appropriate-no-high-frequency.md`: Do not add sound to high-frequency interactions (typing, keyboard navigation).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/appropriate-no-punishing.md`: Sound should inform, not punish; avoid harsh sounds for user mistakes.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/container-callback-ref.md`: Use a callback ref (not useRef) for measurement hooks so the observer attaches when the DOM node is ready.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/container-guard-initial-zero.md`: On initial render, measured bounds are 0. Guard against this to prevent animating from 0 to actual size.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/container-no-excessive-use.md`: Animated bounds is a subtle effect. Use it for buttons, accordions, and interactive elements — not everywhere.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/container-overflow-hidden.md`: Set overflow: hidden on the animated outer container to clip content during size transitions.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/container-transition-delay.md`: Add a small delay to container size animations so the transition feels like it's catching up to the content.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/container-two-div-pattern.md`: Use an outer animated div and an inner measured div. Never measure and animate the same element.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/container-use-resize-observer.md`: Use ResizeObserver to track element dimensions. It fires on resize without causing layout thrashing.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/context-cleanup-nodes.md`: Disconnect and clean up audio nodes after playback.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/context-resume-suspended.md`: Check and resume suspended AudioContext before playing.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/context-reuse-single.md`: Reuse a single AudioContext instance; do not create new ones per sound.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/design-filter-for-character.md`: Apply bandpass filter to shape percussive sounds.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/design-noise-for-percussion.md`: Use filtered noise for clicks/taps, not oscillators.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/design-oscillator-for-tonal.md`: Use oscillators with pitch movement for tonal sounds (pops, confirmations).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/duration-max-300ms.md`: User-initiated animations must not exceed 300ms.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/duration-press-hover.md`: Press and hover interactions should use 120-180ms duration.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/duration-shorten-before-curve.md`: If animation feels slow, shorten duration before adjusting curve.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/duration-small-state.md`: Small state changes should use 180-260ms duration.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/easing-entrance-ease-out.md`: Entrances must use ease-out (arrive fast, settle gently).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/easing-exit-ease-in.md`: Exits must use ease-in (build momentum before departure).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/easing-for-state-change.md`: System-initiated state changes should use easing curves.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/easing-linear-only-progress.md`: Linear easing only for progress bars and time representation.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/easing-natural-decay.md`: Use exponential ramps, not linear, for natural decay.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/easing-no-linear-motion.md`: Linear easing should only be used for progress indicators, not motion.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/easing-transition-ease-in-out.md`: View/mode transitions use ease-in-out for neutral attention.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/envelope-exponential-decay.md`: Use exponential ramps for natural decay, not linear.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/envelope-no-zero-target.md`: Exponential ramps cannot target 0; use 0.001 or similar small value.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/envelope-set-initial-value.md`: Set initial value before ramping to avoid glitches.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/exit-key-required.md`: Dynamic lists inside AnimatePresence must have unique keys.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/exit-matches-initial.md`: Exit animation should mirror initial for symmetry.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/exit-prop-required.md`: Elements inside AnimatePresence should have exit prop defined.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/exit-requires-wrapper.md`: Conditional motion elements must be wrapped in AnimatePresence.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/impl-default-subtle.md`: Default volume should be subtle, not loud.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/impl-preload-audio.md`: Preload audio files to avoid playback delay.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/impl-reset-current-time.md`: Reset audio currentTime before replay to allow rapid triggering.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/mode-pop-layout-for-lists.md`: Use popLayout mode for list reordering animations.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/mode-sync-layout-conflict.md`: Mode "sync" causes layout conflicts; position exiting elements absolutely.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/mode-wait-doubles-duration.md`: Mode "wait" nearly doubles animation duration; adjust timing accordingly.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-aria-hidden.md`: Icon SVGs should be aria-hidden since they're decorative.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-consistent-viewbox.md`: All icons must use the same viewBox (14x14 recommended).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-group-variants.md`: Icons that are rotational variants MUST share the same group and base lines.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-jump-non-grouped.md`: When transitioning between icons NOT in the same group, rotation should jump instantly.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-reduced-motion.md`: Respect prefers-reduced-motion by disabling animations.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-spring-rotation.md`: Rotation between grouped icons should use spring physics for natural motion.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-strokelinecap-round.md`: Lines should use strokeLinecap="round" for polished endpoints.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-three-lines.md`: Every icon MUST use exactly 3 lines. No more, no fewer.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/morphing-use-collapsed.md`: Unused lines must use the collapsed constant, not omission or null.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/native-backdrop-styling.md`: Use ::backdrop pseudo-element for dialog/popover backgrounds.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/native-placeholder-styling.md`: Use ::placeholder for input placeholder styling, not wrapper elements.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/native-selection-styling.md`: Use ::selection for text selection styling.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/nested-consistent-timing.md`: Parent and child exit durations should be coordinated.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/nested-propagate-required.md`: Nested AnimatePresence must use propagate prop for coordinated exits.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/none-context-menu-entrance.md`: Context menus should not animate on entrance (exit only).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/none-high-frequency.md`: High-frequency interactions should have no animation.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/none-keyboard-navigation.md`: Keyboard navigation should be instant, no animation.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/param-click-duration.md`: Click/tap sounds should be 5-15ms duration.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/param-filter-frequency-range.md`: Bandpass filter for clicks should be 3000-6000Hz.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/param-q-value-range.md`: Filter Q for clicks should be 2-5 for focused but not harsh sound.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/param-reasonable-gain.md`: Gain values should not exceed 1.0 to prevent clipping.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/physics-active-state.md`: Interactive elements must have active/pressed state with scale transform.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/physics-no-excessive-stagger.md`: Stagger delays must not exceed 50ms per item.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/physics-spring-for-overshoot.md`: Use springs (not easing) when overshoot-and-settle is needed.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/physics-subtle-deformation.md`: Squash/stretch deformation must be subtle (0.95-1.05 range).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/prefetch-hit-slop.md`: Expand the invisible prediction area around elements with hitSlop to start loading sooner.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/prefetch-keyboard-tab.md`: Monitor focus changes and prefetch when the user is a few tab stops away from a registered element.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/prefetch-not-everything.md`: Don't prefetch everything visible in the viewport. Prefetch based on user intent to avoid wasted bandwidth.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/prefetch-touch-fallback.md`: Touch devices have no cursor. Fall back to viewport or touch-start strategies automatically.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/prefetch-trajectory-over-hover.md`: Hover prefetching starts too late. Trajectory prediction fires while the cursor is still in motion, reclaiming 100-200ms.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/prefetch-use-selectively.md`: Predictive prefetching doesn't belong in every project. Use it where navigation latency is noticeable.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/presence-disable-interactions.md`: Disable interactions on exiting elements using isPresent.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/presence-hook-in-child.md`: useIsPresent must be called from child of AnimatePresence, not parent.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/presence-safe-to-remove.md`: When using usePresence, always call safeToRemove after async work.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/pseudo-content-required.md`: ::before and ::after require content property to render.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/pseudo-first-line-styling.md`: Use ::first-line for drop-cap-adjacent styling without JavaScript or hardcoded spans.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/pseudo-hit-target-expansion.md`: Use negative inset values to expand hit targets without extra markup.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/pseudo-marker-styling.md`: Use ::marker to style list bullets without extra elements or background-image hacks.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/pseudo-over-dom-node.md`: Use pseudo-elements for decorative content instead of extra DOM nodes.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/pseudo-position-relative-parent.md`: Parent must have position: relative for absolute pseudo-elements.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/pseudo-z-index-layering.md`: Pseudo-elements need z-index to layer correctly with content.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/spring-for-gestures.md`: Gesture-driven motion (drag, flick, swipe) must use springs.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/spring-for-interruptible.md`: Motion that can be interrupted must use springs.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/spring-params-balanced.md`: Spring parameters must be balanced; avoid excessive oscillation.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/spring-preserves-velocity.md`: When velocity matters, use springs to preserve input energy.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/staging-dim-background.md`: Modal/dialog backgrounds should dim to direct focus.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/staging-one-focal-point.md`: Only one element should animate prominently at a time.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/staging-z-index-hierarchy.md`: Animated elements must respect z-index layering.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/timing-consistent.md`: Similar elements must use identical timing values.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/timing-no-entrance-context-menu.md`: Context menus should not animate on entrance (exit only).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/timing-under-300ms.md`: User-initiated animations must complete within 300ms.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/transition-name-cleanup.md`: Remove view-transition-name after transition completes.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/transition-name-required.md`: Elements participating in view transitions need view-transition-name.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/transition-name-unique.md`: Each view-transition-name must be unique on the page during transition.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/transition-over-js-library.md`: Prefer View Transitions API over JavaScript animation libraries for page transitions.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/transition-style-pseudo-elements.md`: Style view transition pseudo-elements for custom animations.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-antialiased-on-retina.md`: Set -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased on retina displays. The default subpixel rendering looks thicker and fuzzier.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-disambiguation-stylistic-set.md`: Enable ss02 (or your font's disambiguation set) in code-facing UIs to distinguish I, l, 1 and 0, O.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-font-display-swap.md`: Set font-display: swap so text renders immediately with a fallback font while the custom font loads.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-justify-with-hyphens.md`: Justified text without hyphens creates rivers of whitespace. Always pair with hyphens: auto.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-letter-spacing-uppercase.md`: Uppercase and small-caps text needs positive letter-spacing to feel open and readable.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-no-font-synthesis.md`: Set font-synthesis: none to prevent the browser from faking bold or italic. Browser-generated faux styles look terrible.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-oldstyle-nums-for-prose.md`: Use oldstyle-nums in body text so numbers blend with lowercase letters. Use lining-nums in tables and headings.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-opentype-contextual-alternates.md`: Keep contextual alternates enabled (calt). They adjust punctuation and glyph shapes based on surrounding characters.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-optical-sizing-auto.md`: Leave font-optical-sizing at auto. The font adjusts glyph shapes for the current size — thicker strokes at small sizes, finer details at large sizes.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-proper-fractions.md`: Enable diagonal-fractions to convert 1/2, 1/3, etc. into proper typographic fractions.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-slashed-zero.md`: Enable slashed zero in code-adjacent UIs so users never confuse 0 with O.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-tabular-nums-for-data.md`: Use tabular-nums for any numeric data that should align in columns (tables, dashboards, pricing).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-text-wrap-balance-headings.md`: Use text-wrap: balance on headings to make lines roughly equal length instead of one long line and a short orphan.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-text-wrap-pretty.md`: Use text-wrap: pretty for body text to reduce orphans. Use text-wrap: balance for headings.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-underline-offset.md`: Use text-underline-offset to push underlines below descenders so they look intentional.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/type-variable-weight-continuous.md`: Variable fonts accept any integer from 100-900, not just the standard stops at 400, 500, 600, 700.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-aesthetic-usability.md`: Users perceive aesthetically pleasing design as more usable. Small visual details compound into trust.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-cognitive-load-reduce.md`: Remove anything that doesn't help the user complete their task. Decoration, redundant labels, and unnecessary options all add load.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-common-region-boundaries.md`: Elements sharing a clearly defined boundary are perceived as a group.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-doherty-perceived-speed.md`: If you can't make something fast, make it feel fast with optimistic UI, skeletons, or progress indicators.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-doherty-under-400ms.md`: Interactions must respond within 400ms to feel instant. Above this threshold, users notice delay.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-fitts-hit-area.md`: Use pseudo-elements or invisible padding to expand clickable areas beyond visible bounds.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-fitts-target-size.md`: The bigger something is, the easier it is to click. Make interactive elements large enough to hit comfortably.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-goal-gradient-progress.md`: People accelerate behavior as they approach a goal. Show how close they are to finishing.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-hicks-minimize-choices.md`: Decision time increases logarithmically with the number of choices. Use progressive disclosure.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-jakobs-familiar-patterns.md`: Users spend most of their time on other sites. They expect yours to work the same way (Jakob's Law).
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-millers-chunking.md`: Working memory holds about 7 items. Group and chunk large data sets so they're scannable.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-pareto-prioritize-features.md`: 80% of users use 20% of features (Pareto Principle). Optimize the critical path first.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-peak-end-finish-strong.md`: People judge experiences by their peak moment and their end. Invest in success and completion states.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-postels-accept-messy-input.md`: Inputs should accept messy human data and normalize it. Validate generously, format strictly.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-pragnanz-simplify.md`: People interpret complex visuals as the simplest form possible. Reduce visual noise to aid comprehension.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-progressive-disclosure.md`: Don't overwhelm users with everything at once. Reveal complexity incrementally as needed.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-proximity-grouping.md`: Elements near each other are perceived as related. Use spacing to create visual groups.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-serial-position.md`: Users best remember the first and last items in a sequence. Place the most important actions at these positions.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-similarity-consistency.md`: Elements that function the same should look the same. Visual consistency signals functional consistency.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-teslers-complexity.md`: Every system has irreducible complexity. The question is who handles it — the user or the system.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-uniform-connectedness.md`: Elements that are visually connected (by lines, color, or frames) are perceived as more related.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-von-restorff-emphasis.md`: When multiple similar elements are present, the one that differs is most likely to be remembered.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/ux-zeigarnik-show-incomplete.md`: People remember incomplete tasks better than completed ones. Use this to drive engagement.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-animate-shadow-pseudo.md`: Transitioning box-shadow directly forces expensive repaints. Instead, put the target shadow on a pseudo-element and animate its opacity.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-border-alpha-colors.md`: Semi-transparent borders adapt to any background color and create subtle, non-jarring separation.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-button-shadow-anatomy.md`: A polished button uses six layered techniques, not just a single box-shadow.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-concentric-radius.md`: When nesting rounded elements, inner radius must equal outer radius minus the gap. Same radius on both creates uneven curves.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-consistent-spacing-scale.md`: Don't use arbitrary pixel values for spacing. Define a scale and stick to it throughout the UI.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-layered-shadows.md`: A single box-shadow looks flat. Layer multiple shadows with increasing blur and decreasing opacity to mimic real light.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-no-pure-black-shadow.md`: Pure black shadows look harsh and artificial. Use deep neutrals or semi-transparent dark colors.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-shadow-direction.md`: All shadows must share the same offset direction to imply a single light source. Mixed directions feel broken.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/visual-shadow-matches-elevation.md`: Larger blur and offset means higher elevation. Use a consistent shadow scale across your UI.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/weight-duration-matches-action.md`: Sound duration should match action duration.
- `.claude/skills/userinterface-wiki/rules/weight-match-action.md`: Sound weight should match action importance.

