- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/animation-derived-value.md`: When deriving a shared value from another, use `useDerivedValue` instead of dependencies, and return a value you can use directly. Animated reactions are for side effects, not derivations.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/animation-gesture-detector-press.md`: For animated press states (scale, opacity on press), use `GestureDetector` with JS thread round-trip for press animations.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/animation-gpu-properties.md`: Avoid animating `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`, `margin`, or `padding`. These trigger layout recalculation on every frame. Instead, use `transform` (scale, translate) and `opacity` which run on the GPU without triggering layout.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/design-system-compound-components.md`: Don't create components that can accept a string if they aren't a text node. If a component can receive a string child, it must be a dedicated `*Text` component. For components like buttons, which can have both a View (or Pressable) together with text, use compound components, such a `Button`,
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/fonts-config-plugin.md`: Use the `expo-font` config plugin to embed fonts at build time instead of
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/imports-design-system-folder.md`: Re-export dependencies from a design system folder. App code imports from there, not directly from packages. This enables global changes and easy refactoring.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/js-hoist-intl.md`: Don't create `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, `Intl.NumberFormat`, or instantiate. Hoist to module scope when the locale/options are static.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-callbacks.md`: **Impact: HIGH (Fewer re-renders and faster lists)**
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-function-references.md`: Don't map or filter data before passing to virtualized lists. Virtualization relies on object reference stability to know what changed—new references cause full re-renders of all visible items. Attempt to prevent frequent renders at the list-parent level.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-images.md`: Always load compressed, appropriately-sized images in lists. Full-resolution images consume excessive memory and cause scroll jank. Request thumbnails from your server or use an image CDN with resize parameters.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-inline-objects.md`: Don't create new objects inside `renderItem` to pass as props. Inline objects create new references on every render, breaking memoization. Pass primitive values directly from `item` instead.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-item-expensive.md`: List items should be as inexpensive as possible to render. Minimize hooks, avoid queries, and limit React Context access. Virtualized lists render many items during scroll—expensive items cause jank.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-item-memo.md`: When possible, pass only primitive values (strings, numbers, booleans) as props to list item components. Primitives enable shallow comparison in `memo()` to work correctly, skipping re-renders when values haven't changed.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-item-types.md`: When a list has different item layouts (messages, images, headers, etc.), use a into separate recycling pools so a message component never gets recycled into an image component.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/list-performance-virtualize.md`: Use a list virtualizer like LegendList or FlashList instead of ScrollView with mapped children—even for short lists. Virtualizers only render visible items, reducing memory usage and mount time. ScrollView renders all children upfront, which gets expensive quickly.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/monorepo-native-deps-in-app.md`: In a monorepo, packages with native code must be installed in the native app's directory directly. Autolinking only scans the app's `node_modules`—it won't find native dependencies installed in other packages.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/monorepo-single-dependency-versions.md`: Use a single version of each dependency across all packages in your monorepo. Prefer exact versions over ranges. Multiple versions cause duplicate code in bundles, runtime conflicts, and inconsistent behavior across packages.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/navigation-native-navigators.md`: Always use native navigators instead of JS-based ones. Native navigators use platform APIs (UINavigationController on iOS, Fragment on Android) for better performance and native behavior.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/react-compiler-destructure-functions.md`: This rule is only applicable if you are using the React Compiler.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/react-compiler-reanimated-shared-values.md`: With React Compiler enabled, use `.get()` and `.set()` instead of reading or writing `.value` directly on Reanimated shared values. The compiler can't track property access—explicit methods ensure correct behavior.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/react-state-dispatcher.md`: When the next state depends on the current state, use a dispatch updater (`setState(prev => ...)`) instead of reading the state variable directly in a callback. This avoids stale closures and ensures you're comparing against the latest value.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/react-state-fallback.md`: Use `undefined` as initial state and nullish coalescing (`??`) to fall back to parent or server values. State represents user intent only—`undefined` means "user hasn't chosen yet." This enables reactive fallbacks that update when the source changes, not just on initial render.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/react-state-minimize.md`: Use the fewest state variables possible. If a value can be computed from existing state or props, derive it during render instead of storing it in state. Redundant state causes unnecessary re-renders and can drift out of sync.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/rendering-no-falsy-and.md`: Never use `{value && <Component />}` when `value` could be an empty string or text outside a `<Text>` component, causing a hard crash in production.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/rendering-text-in-text-component.md`: Strings must be rendered inside `<Text>`. React Native crashes if a string is a direct child of `<View>`.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/scroll-position-no-state.md`: Never store scroll position in `useState`. Scroll events fire rapidly—state updates cause render thrashing and dropped frames. Use a Reanimated shared value for animations or a ref for non-reactive tracking.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/state-ground-truth.md`: State variables—both React `useState` and Reanimated shared values—should represent the actual state of something (e.g., `pressed`, `progress`, `isOpen`), not derived visual values (e.g., `scale`, `opacity`, `translateY`). Derive visual values from state using computation or interpolation.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-expo-image.md`: Use `expo-image` instead of React Native's `Image`. It provides memory-efficient caching, blurhash placeholders, progressive loading, and better performance for lists.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-image-gallery.md`: For image galleries with lightbox (tap to fullscreen), use `@nandorojo/galeria`. It provides native shared element transitions with pinch-to-zoom, double-tap zoom, and pan-to-close. Works with any image component including `expo-image`.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-measure-views.md`: Use both `useLayoutEffect` (synchronous) and `onLayout` (for updates). The sync measurement gives you the initial size immediately; `onLayout` keeps it current when the view changes. For non-primitive states, use a dispatch updater to compare values and avoid unnecessary re-renders.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-menus.md`: Use native platform menus instead of custom JS implementations. Native menus provide built-in accessibility, consistent platform UX, and better performance. Use [zeego](https://zeego.dev) for cross-platform native menus.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-native-modals.md`: Use native `<Modal>` with `presentationStyle="formSheet"` or React Navigation v7's native form sheet instead of JS-based bottom sheet libraries. Native modals have built-in gestures, accessibility, and better performance. Rely on native UI for low-level primitives.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-pressable.md`: Never use `TouchableOpacity` or `TouchableHighlight`. Use `Pressable` from
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-safe-area-scroll.md`: Use `contentInsetAdjustmentBehavior="automatic"` on the root ScrollView instead of wrapping content in SafeAreaView or manual padding. This lets iOS handle safe area insets natively with proper scroll behavior.
- `.claude/skills/vercel-react-native-skills/rules/ui-scrollview-content-inset.md`: When adding space to the top or bottom of a ScrollView that may change (keyboard, toolbars, dynamic content), use `contentInset` instead of padding. Changing `contentInset` doesn't trigger layout recalculation—it adjusts the scroll area without re-rendering content.
