- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/teleport-ssr-hydration.md`: **Impact: HIGH** - Teleports require special handling during SSR. The teleported content is not part of the server-rendered HTML string, causing hydration mismatches that can break the application or cause content to disappear.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/teleport-target-must-exist.md`: **Impact: HIGH** - The teleport `to` target must already exist in the DOM when the `<Teleport>` component is mounted. If the target doesn't exist, Vue will throw an error and the teleported content won't render.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/template-expressions-restrictions.md`: **Impact: MEDIUM** - Vue templates only support single JavaScript expressions, not statements. Using variable declarations, if statements, or multiple statements will cause template compilation errors.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/template-functions-no-side-effects.md`: **Impact: MEDIUM** - Functions called in templates execute on every component re-render. Functions with side effects (modifying data, API calls, logging) will cause unpredictable behavior, performance issues, and difficult-to-debug bugs.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/template-ref-null-with-v-if.md`: **Impact: MEDIUM** - When using template refs with `v-if`, the ref becomes `null` when the element is unmounted. Watchers and effects that access these refs must handle the null case to avoid runtime errors.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/template-ref-unwrapping-top-level.md`: **Impact: MEDIUM** - Vue only auto-unwraps refs that are top-level properties in the template render context. Nested refs (refs inside objects) are NOT unwrapped in expressions, causing `[object Object]` rendering or calculation errors.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/template-ref-v-for-order.md`: **Impact: MEDIUM** - When using template refs inside `v-for`, Vue collects the element references into an array. However, this array does NOT guarantee the same order as the source array. Relying on index-based access can lead to subtle bugs.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/textarea-no-interpolation.md`: **Impact: HIGH** - Interpolation in textarea (`{{ text }}`) provides one-way binding only - it displays the initial value but user input does NOT update the ref. This creates a confusing disconnect where the textarea shows content but edits are silently lost.
