- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/watcheffect-async-dependency-tracking.md`: **Impact: HIGH** - `watchEffect` automatically tracks reactive dependencies, but only during synchronous execution. Any reactive properties accessed after the first `await` statement will NOT be tracked, and changes to them won't trigger the watcher.
- `.claude/skills/vue-best-practices/reference/watcheffect-flush-post-for-refs.md`: **Impact: MEDIUM** - By default, `watchEffect` runs before the DOM is updated. When watching template refs, this means the effect may run with stale or null ref values. Use `flush: 'post'` to ensure the effect runs after DOM updates when refs are current.
