- `.claude/skills/vue-debug-guides/reference/ssr-hydration-mismatch-causes.md`: **Impact: HIGH** - Hydration mismatches occur when the HTML rendered on the client differs from what the server rendered. Vue attempts to recover by discarding and re-rendering mismatched nodes, causing performance degradation, visual flickering, and potentially broken event handlers.
- `.claude/skills/vue-debug-guides/reference/ssr-platform-specific-apis.md`: **Impact: HIGH** - SSR applications run the same code on both server (Node.js) and client (browser). Browser APIs like `window`, `document`, and `localStorage` don't exist in Node.js and will throw `ReferenceError`. Similarly, Node.js APIs like `fs` and `process` aren't available in browsers.
