## VueUse Functions

Apply VueUse composables where appropriate to build concise, maintainable Vue.js / Nuxt features.

- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/SKILL.md`
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/computedAsync.md`: Computed for async functions.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/computedEager.md`: Eager computed without lazy evaluation.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/computedInject.md`: Combine `computed` and `inject`. Useful for creating a computed property based on an injected value.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/computedWithControl.md`: Explicitly define the dependencies of computed.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createEventHook.md`: Utility for creating event hooks
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createGenericProjection.md`: Generic version of `createProjection`. Accepts a custom projector function to map arbitrary type of domains.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createGlobalState.md`: Keep states in the global scope to be reusable across Vue instances.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createInjectionState.md`: Create global state that can be injected into components.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createProjection.md`: Reactive numeric projection from one domain to another.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createRef.md`: Returns a `deepRef` or `shallowRef` depending on the `deep` param.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createReusableTemplate.md`: Define and reuse template inside the component scope.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createSharedComposable.md`: Make a composable function usable with multiple Vue instances.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createTemplatePromise.md`: Template as Promise. Useful for constructing custom Dialogs, Modals, Toasts, etc.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/createUnrefFn.md`: Make a plain function accepting ref and raw values as arguments. Returns the same value the unconverted function returns, with proper typing.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/extendRef.md`: Add extra attributes to Ref.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/from.md`: Wrappers around RxJS's [`from()`](https://rxjs.dev/api/index/function/from) and [`fromEvent()`](https://rxjs.dev/api/index/function/fromEvent) to allow them to accept `ref`s.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/get.md`: Shorthand for accessing `ref.value`
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/injectLocal.md`: Extended `inject` with ability to call `provideLocal` to provide the value in the same component.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/isDefined.md`: Non-nullish checking type guard for Ref.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/logicAnd.md`
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/logicNot.md`
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/logicOr.md`
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/makeDestructurable.md`: Make isomorphic destructurable for object and array at the same time. See [this blog](https://antfu.me/posts/destructuring-with-object-or-array/) for more details.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/onClickOutside.md`: Listen for clicks outside of an element. Useful for modals or dropdowns.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/onElementRemoval.md`: Fires when the element or any element containing it is removed from the DOM.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/onKeyStroke.md`: Listen for keyboard keystrokes. By default, listens on `keydown` events on `window`.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/onLongPress.md`: Listen for a long press on an element. Returns a stop function.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/onStartTyping.md`: Fires when users start typing on non-editable elements. Useful for auto-focusing an input field when the user starts typing anywhere on the page.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/provideLocal.md`: Extended `provide` with ability to call `injectLocal` to obtain the value in the same component.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/reactify.md`: Converts plain functions into reactive functions. The converted function accepts refs as its arguments and returns a ComputedRef, with proper typing.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/reactifyObject.md`: Apply `reactify` to an object
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/reactiveComputed.md`: Computed reactive object. Instead of returning a ref that `computed` does, `reactiveComputed` returns a reactive object.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/reactiveOmit.md`: Reactively omit fields from a reactive object.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/reactivePick.md`: Reactively pick fields from a reactive object.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/refAutoReset.md`: A ref which will be reset to the default value after some time.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/refDebounced.md`: Debounce execution of a ref value.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/refDefault.md`: Apply default value to a ref.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/refManualReset.md`: Create a ref with manual reset functionality.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/refThrottled.md`: Throttle changing of a ref value.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/refWithControl.md`: Fine-grained controls over ref and its reactivity.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/set.md`: Shorthand for `ref.value = x`
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/syncRef.md`: Two-way refs synchronization.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/syncRefs.md`: Keep target refs in sync with a source ref
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/templateRef.md`: ::: info This function will be removed in future version.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/toObserver.md`: Sugar function to convert a `ref` into an RxJS [Observer](https://rxjs.dev/guide/observer).
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/toReactive.md`: Converts ref to reactive. Also made possible to create a "swapable" reactive object.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/toRef.md`: Normalize value/ref/getter to `ref` or `computed`.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/toRefs.md`: Extended [`toRefs`](https://vuejs.org/api/reactivity-utilities.html#torefs) that also accepts refs of an object.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/tryOnBeforeMount.md`: Safe `onBeforeMount`. Call `onBeforeMount()` if it's inside a component lifecycle, if not, just call the function
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/tryOnBeforeUnmount.md`: Safe `onBeforeUnmount`. Call `onBeforeUnmount()` if it's inside a component lifecycle, if not, do nothing
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/tryOnMounted.md`: Safe `onMounted`. Call `onMounted()` if it's inside a component lifecycle, if not, just call the function
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/tryOnScopeDispose.md`: Safe `onScopeDispose`. Call `onScopeDispose()` if it's inside an effect scope lifecycle, if not, do nothing
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/tryOnUnmounted.md`: Safe `onUnmounted`. Call `onUnmounted()` if it's inside a component lifecycle, if not, do nothing
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/unrefElement.md`: Retrieves the underlying DOM element from a Vue ref or component instance
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/until.md`: Promised one-time watch for changes
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/useAbs.md`: Reactive `Math.abs`.
- `.claude/skills/vueuse-functions/references/useActiveElement.md`: Reactive `document.activeElement`. Returns a shallow ref that updates when focus changes.
